:"note","label":"Situation","text":"Political tensions are increasing in a region with a history of ethnic conflict."},{"type":"p","text":"A Conflict Analyst should assess:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Historical Drivers","Current Actors","Trigger Events","Conflict Indicators","Escalation Risks","Humanitarian Impact","Possible Scenarios","Mitigation Options"]},{"type":"p","text":"The analyst should distinguish clearly between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Verified facts"},{"text":"Credible but unconfirmed information"},{"text":"Analytical assessment"},{"text":"Forecast"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This distinction is essential in professional conflict analysis."},{"type":"h","text":"Analytical Framework"},{"type":"p","text":"A useful professional workflow is:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Context"},{"type":"p","text":"What is happening?"},{"type":"h","text":"2. Actors"},{"type":"p","text":"Who is involved?"},{"type":"h","text":"3. Interests"},{"type":"p","text":"What does each actor want?"},{"type":"h","text":"4. Drivers"},{"type":"p","text":"Why is the conflict occurring?"},{"type":"h","text":"5. Triggers"},{"type":"p","text":"What could rapidly escalate it?"},{"type":"h","text":"6. Indicators"},{"type":"p","text":"What signals suggest deterioration or improvement?"},{"type":"h","text":"7. Scenarios"},{"type":"p","text":"What could happen next?"},{"type":"h","text":"8. Recommendations"},{"type":"p","text":"What actions could reduce risk?"},{"type":"h","text":"Government / Public-Sector Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Foreign affairs"},{"text":"Internal security"},{"text":"Defence and strategic affairs"},{"text":"Human rights"},{"text":"Disaster and humanitarian response"},{"text":"Refugee and migration policy"},{"text":"Development programmes"},{"text":"Public policy"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible pathways include competitive government examinations, research organisations, policy institutions and specialised recruitment."},{"type":"p","text":"Specific government positions have post-specific educational, examination, experience and eligibility requirements."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A postgraduate degree is strongly recommended for a dedicated Conflict Analyst career."},{"type":"table","header":["PG","Best For"],"rows":[[{"text":"MA Peace & Conflict Studies"},{"text":"Direct conflict specialisation"}],[{"text":"MA International Relations"},{"text":"Geopolitical analysis"}],[{"text":"MA International Security"},{"text":"Security analysis"}],[{"text":"MA Human Rights"},{"text":"Rights-based analysis"}],[{"text":"MA Political Science"},{"text":"Political/conflict research"}],[{"text":"MA Defence & Strategic Studies"},{"text":"Security and defence"}],[{"text":"MA Public Policy"},{"text":"Policy analysis"}],[{"text":"MA Development Studies"},{"text":"Conflict-development"}],[{"text":"MA Sociology"},{"text":"Social conflict"}],[{"text":"MA Disaster Management"},{"text":"Humanitarian/crisis work"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong Route"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Peace & Conflict Studies","Conflict Research Internship","MA Peace & Conflict / International Security","Research Assistant","Conflict Analyst"]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"United Kingdom"},{"text":"United States"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Switzerland"},{"text":"France"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Norway"},{"text":"Ireland"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential programmes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Peace & Conflict Studies"},{"text":"International Security"},{"text":"Conflict Resolution"},{"text":"Human Rights"},{"text":"International Relations"},{"text":"Security Studies"},{"text":"Humanitarian Studies"},{"text":"Development Studies"},{"text":"Peacebuilding"}]},{"type":"p","text":