els"},{"text":"Geospatial risk analysis"},{"text":"Large-scale media analysis"},{"text":"Humanitarian forecasting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should support—not replace—human analytical judgment, especially when evidence is incomplete or politically contested."},{"type":"h","text":"Future Skills — 2030+"},{"type":"p","text":"The Conflict Analyst of the future will increasingly combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Conflict Theory","Geopolitics","Data","OSINT","GIS","AI","Policy"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Important skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Geospatial intelligence"},{"text":"OSINT"},{"text":"Conflict-event databases"},{"text":"Satellite imagery analysis"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Scenario modelling"},{"text":"Early-warning systems"},{"text":"Digital verification"},{"text":"Information-warfare analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Outlook"},{"type":"p","text":"Conflict analysis is likely to become increasingly data-driven and technology-enabled."},{"type":"p","text":"Future analysts may work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Real-time conflict dashboards"},{"text":"Satellite imagery"},{"text":"AI-based early-warning systems"},{"text":"Social-media signals"},{"text":"Climate models"},{"text":"Migration forecasts"},{"text":"Cyber-threat indicators"},{"text":"Digital disinformation monitoring"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The human analyst remains responsible for context, source evaluation, uncertainty, ethics and policy judgment."},{"type":"h","text":"Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Conflict & Security"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Conflict theory"},{"text":"Geopolitics"},{"text":"International security"},{"text":"Peacebuilding"},{"text":"Human rights"},{"text":"Mediation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Field research"},{"text":"Interview methods"},{"text":"Content analysis"},{"text":"Po